CODECS(1)                   User Commands                  CODECS(1)

NAME
    codecs - list, identify and convert image and audio formats

SYNOPSIS
    codecs
    codecs info file...
    codecs convert [-f name] [-b bits] [-s size] in out

DESCRIPTION
    The formats of minios are modules in /lib/codecs, which the codec
    library loads at run time; every program that opens images or
    audio reads the formats of all modules. The environment variable
    CODEC_PATH names another module directory.

    Without arguments codecs lists every codec with its capabilities
    (D decodes, E encodes, S renders at any size), its kind, its
    module, its description, its MIME types and its extensions.

    info names the format of each file, found by its content and then
    by its extension, and describes it: the size of an image and
    whether it has alpha, or the rate, channels, sample size, frames
    and duration of audio.

    convert decodes in and encodes it in the format of the extension of
    out, or with the codec name. Both formats must be of one kind.

OPTIONS
    -f name      encode with this codec, whatever the extension
    -b bits      sample size of the converted audio (the source's)
    -s size      size in pixels at which a vector image is rendered

EXIT STATUS
    0 on success, 1 when a file cannot be read, identified, decoded,
    encoded or written, and 2 for wrong usage.

EXAMPLES
    codecs
    codecs info /usr/share/sounds/chime.wav
    codecs convert shot.png shot.bmp
    codecs convert -s 64 /usr/share/icons/app-default.svg icon.png
    codecs convert -b 24 chime.wav chime24.wav

SEE ALSO
    screenshot(1)
